  "instructions": [
    "Bring the water and 1 tbsp salt to a boil in a large pot over high heat.",
    "Heat the olive oil in a deep 12-inch skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and carrots and cook 5 minutes, until soft.",
    "Stir in the garlic and cook 30 seconds. Add the ground beef and break it into small crumbles.",
    "Cook the beef 6 to 8 minutes, until no pink remains and it reaches 160 F.",
    "Stir in the crushed tomatoes, oregano, 1 tsp salt, and pepper. Simmer on medium-low 12 minutes, stirring now and then, until thick.",
    "While the sauce simmers, cook the spaghetti in the boiling water for the time on the package, usually 8 to 10 minutes, until tender. Save 1/2 cup of the pasta water if you like, then drain.",
    "Toss the spaghetti in the skillet with the sauce for 1 minute, until coated. Serve hot. To freeze, cool the pasta and sauce fully and store in airtight containers for up to 3 months."
  ],
